  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) has been completed, yielding accuracy 0.485 / F1 0.464. This gives us a single unimodal (RNA) baseline but zero information about the image modality's contribution. Uncertainty: The most critical open question for a multimodal study is whether the image modality is informative at all and how it compares to RNA. Without an image-only baseline, any future multimodal result would be uninterpretable—we could not distinguish whether gains come from image features, the fusion mechanism, or simply a stronger unimodal model. What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) establishes the image-only baseline using the simplest, most standard image encoder and the same singleprofile setting as config_001, isolating the modality effect. Why this is the best next experiment: It reduces the highest-impact uncertainty with a clean, minimal-configuration comparison. Once both unimodal baselines are known, subsequent experiments (multiprofile, multimodal fusion, encoder choices) can be interpreted against a well-characterized landscape, making every remaining budget slot more informative."
}

